# Secrets never enter git. Tokens are supplied through the environment.
.env
.env.*
*.token
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig

# Model weights are large and are fetched, not committed.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
models/**/weights/

# Local scratch
.DS_Store
tmp/
*.log

# Benchmark raw output that has not been curated into a dated result directory
bench/raw/

# Agent working notes. Task briefs, per-batch reports, and review diffs from
# the phase 1 build. Nothing here was ever tracked (confirmed 2026-08-19 with
# `git ls-files .superpowers`, which returned nothing), so this rule only
# stops the directory appearing in `git status`. CLAUDE.md's "Working notes"
# section points at it, and that pointer only resolves on a machine that has
# the directory - it does not arrive with a clone.
.superpowers/

# Design and planning documents written during the build. Untracked on
# 2026-08-19 by request, with `git rm --cached -r docs/superpowers`; the files
# stay on disk. Anything in here that has to survive a clone belongs in an ADR
# (docs/adr/), in README.md, or in a code comment. Every reference to
# this directory that remains in a tracked file is marked "local working
# document, not in git" so nobody follows a pointer a clone cannot resolve.
docs/superpowers/

# Untracked on 2026-08-19 by request, with `git rm --cached`. Before it was
# removed its load-bearing records were moved into tracked homes, so nothing
# was lost with it: the nine phase 1 acceptance criteria and the proven/unproven
# account are in README.md, the predicted sync-wave defect is a comment in
# tests/smoke/10-gitops.bats, the two dry-run defects are in CLAUDE.md's
# evidence rules, and the CI untried records are in the workflow itself.
# Owed measurements were never centralised there anyway - each lives beside
# the claim it qualifies, findable with
# `grep -rn '\*\*Unmeasured (20' . --exclude-dir=.git --exclude-dir=docs/superpowers`.
docs/UNVERIFIED.md
